# Shell scripts must keep LF endings regardless of the checkout platform. This repo is developed on
# Windows, where `core.autocrlf=true` would otherwise hand macOS a script whose shebang line ends in
# a carriage return — which fails as `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M`.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The bundled assets are binary, said explicitly rather than left to Git's NUL-byte heuristic. This
# repo is developed with core.autocrlf=true, and a single mangled byte in an icon or the hoot is a
# corrupt file that still builds — `include_bytes!` takes whatever is there.
*.png binary
*.mp3 binary

# Source and docs are LF in the index and must stay so. A CRLF flip reads as a full-file rewrite
# in every diff and has landed twice by accident from Windows editors; saying it here makes the
# index normalise whatever the editor did.
*.rs text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
